Wait, that's 4 + 1 + 5 + 1 + 5 + 1 + 5 + 1 = 23 columns. That matches!

So the pattern is groups of 4 {8,3} columns, then 1 {8,6} column, repeat.


The columns with only {8} act as dividers—these are the pillars. Looking at the row structure, I can see there are two main horizontal sections that contain the regular content, while the top and bottom rows contain only the pillar columns without any content in between.

The output should represent the character at each corner intersection of these sections—so positions like top-left, top-right, bottom-left, and bottom-right are the key features to capture.

Given the two regions horizontally and four regions vertically, that gives eight total corners to extract.

